            <ArticleTitle>When size matters: lessons learned from left main stent embolization and retrieval.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>350-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>While the advantages of drug-eluting stents (DES) have been demonstrated in moderate and small-sized vessels, the benefits of DES use in selected larger vessels are increasingly recognized. In the following case presentation, the use of a DES outside the approved vessel diameter to treat left main coronary artery disease led to retrograde migration of the stent over the guiding catheter. Solutions to capturing and retrieving a stent in this position are discussed and our approach to resolving the situation is presented.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
